.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
This page details how to use the libusb hotplug interface, where available\&. 

Be mindful that not all platforms currently implement hotplug notification and that you should first call on \fBlibusb_has_capability()\fP with parameter \fBLIBUSB_CAP_HAS_HOTPLUG\fP to confirm that hotplug support is available\&. 
.SH "Typedef Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "typedef int \fBlibusb_hotplug_callback_handle\fP"

.PP
Callback handle\&. Callbacks handles are generated by \fBlibusb_hotplug_register_callback()\fP and can be used to deregister callbacks\&. Callback handles are unique per \fBlibusb_context\fP and it is safe to call \fBlibusb_hotplug_deregister_callback()\fP on an already deregistered callback\&.

.PP
Since version 1\&.0\&.16, \fBLIBUSB_API_VERSION\fP >= 0x01000102

.PP
For more information, see \fBDevice hotplug event notification\fP\&. 
.SS "typedef int(* libusb_hotplug_callback_fn) (\fBlibusb_context\fP *ctx, \fBlibusb_device\fP *device, \fBlibusb_hotplug_event\fP event, void *user_data)"

.PP
Hotplug callback function type\&. When requesting hotplug event notifications, you pass a pointer to a callback function of this type\&.

.PP
This callback may be called by an internal event thread and as such it is recommended the callback do minimal processing before returning\&.

.PP
libusb will call this function later, when a matching event had happened on a matching device\&. See \fBDevice hotplug event notification\fP for more information\&.

.PP
It is safe to call either \fBlibusb_hotplug_register_callback()\fP or \fBlibusb_hotplug_deregister_callback()\fP from within a callback function\&.

.PP
Since version 1\&.0\&.16, \fBLIBUSB_API_VERSION\fP >= 0x01000102

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIctx\fP context of this notification 
.br
\fIdevice\fP \fBlibusb_device\fP this event occurred on 
.br
\fIevent\fP event that occurred 
.br
\fIuser_data\fP user data provided when this callback was registered 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
bool whether this callback is finished processing events\&. returning 1 will cause this callback to be deregistered 
.RE
.PP

