Arm the callback and fire it for all matching currently attached devices\&. 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "int libusb_hotplug_register_callback (\fBlibusb_context\fP * ctx, int events, int flags, int vendor_id, int product_id, int dev_class, \fBlibusb_hotplug_callback_fn\fP cb_fn, void * user_data, \fBlibusb_hotplug_callback_handle\fP * callback_handle)"

.PP
Register a hotplug callback function\&. Register a callback with the \fBlibusb_context\fP\&. The callback will fire when a matching event occurs on a matching device\&. The callback is armed until either it is deregistered with \fBlibusb_hotplug_deregister_callback()\fP or the supplied callback returns 1 to indicate it is finished processing events\&.

.PP
If the \fBLIBUSB_HOTPLUG_ENUMERATE\fP is passed the callback will be called with a \fBLIBUSB_HOTPLUG_EVENT_DEVICE_ARRIVED\fP for all devices already plugged into the machine\&. Note that libusb modifies its internal device list from a separate thread, while calling hotplug callbacks from \fBlibusb_handle_events()\fP, so it is possible for a device to already be present on, or removed from, its internal device list, while the hotplug callbacks still need to be dispatched\&. This means that when using \fBLIBUSB_HOTPLUG_ENUMERATE\fP, your callback may be called twice for the arrival of the same device, once from \fBlibusb_hotplug_register_callback()\fP and once from \fBlibusb_handle_events()\fP; and/or your callback may be called for the removal of a device for which an arrived call was never made\&.

.PP
Since version 1\&.0\&.16, \fBLIBUSB_API_VERSION\fP >= 0x01000102

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIctx\fP context to register this callback with 
.br
\fIevents\fP bitwise or of hotplug events that will trigger this callback\&. See \fBlibusb_hotplug_event\fP 
.br
\fIflags\fP bitwise or of hotplug flags that affect registration\&. See \fBlibusb_hotplug_flag\fP 
.br
\fIvendor_id\fP the vendor id to match or \fBLIBUSB_HOTPLUG_MATCH_ANY\fP 
.br
\fIproduct_id\fP the product id to match or \fBLIBUSB_HOTPLUG_MATCH_ANY\fP 
.br
\fIdev_class\fP the device class to match or \fBLIBUSB_HOTPLUG_MATCH_ANY\fP 
.br
\fIcb_fn\fP the function to be invoked on a matching event/device 
.br
\fIuser_data\fP user data to pass to the callback function 
.br
\fIcallback_handle\fP pointer to store the handle of the allocated callback (can be NULL) 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
\fBLIBUSB_SUCCESS\fP on success LIBUSB_ERROR code on failure 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void libusb_hotplug_deregister_callback (\fBlibusb_context\fP * ctx, \fBlibusb_hotplug_callback_handle\fP callback_handle)"

.PP
Deregisters a hotplug callback\&. Deregister a callback from a \fBlibusb_context\fP\&. This function is safe to call from within a hotplug callback\&.

.PP
